Step 1 – Create the Python Project

A new Python project was created using PyCharm with Python 3.11.

Step 2 – Create a Virtual Environment

A virtual environment (.venv) was created to isolate the project dependencies from the global Python installation.

Step 3 – Install Required Libraries and ffmpeg 

The following Python packages were installed:

pip install cohere
pip install python-dotenv
pip install RealtimeSTT
pip install "RealtimeSTT[faster-whisper]"
pip install RealtimeTTS
pip install torch
pip install torchaudio
Step 4 – Configure the API Key

A .env file was created to securely store the Cohere API key.

Example:

COHERE_API_KEY=YOUR_API_KEY

The API key is loaded into the application using the python-dotenv library.

Step 5 – Implement Speech-to-Text

The RealtimeSTT library was used to capture audio from the microphone and convert the user's speech into text.

recorder = AudioToTextRecorder()
text = recorder.text()
Step 6 – Connect to Cohere

The recognized text is sent to the Cohere Large Language Model.

response = co.chat(
    model="command-a-03-2025",
    message=text
)

The model processes the user's question and returns an intelligent response.

Step 7 – Implement Text-to-Speech

The generated response is converted into speech using RealtimeTTS.

engine = SystemEngine()
stream = TextToAudioStream(engine)
stream.feed(reply)
stream.play()
Step 8 – Run the Application

After running the program:

The assistant waits for the user to speak.
Speech is converted into text.
The text is sent to Cohere.
Cohere generates a response.
The response is spoken aloud.
The conversation continues until the user says exit.
